<!-- Agent -> MCP tool invocation — Mermaid (retries, error handling) -->

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Agent
  participant MCPClient as "MCP Client (local)"
  participant MCPServer as "MCP Server / Tool"
  participant DB as "State DB"

  Agent->>MCPClient: prepareRequest(tool, input, correlationId)
  MCPClient->>MCPServer: invoke(tool, input)
  alt success
    MCPServer-->>MCPClient: result
    MCPClient-->>Agent: deliver(result)
    Agent->>DB: persist success metadata
  else error
    MCPServer-->>MCPClient: error(code)
    MCPClient-->>Agent: error
    Agent->>Agent: classify error (retriable/non-retriable)
    alt retriable
      Agent->>MCPClient: retry with backoff (1s -> 2s -> 4s)
    else non-retriable
      Agent->>DB: persist failure state, notify operator
    end
  end

  note over Agent,MCPClient
    Best practices:
    - CorrelationId for tracing
    - Circuit-breaker for frequent failures
    - Idempotency keys for tool re-invocations
  end note
```
